kosha link-mass

  -- the mass of a robot link — determines inertia and gravitational load
  --
  -- same concept as mass in physics but scoped to a link entity in a kinematic chain
  -- each link in an n-DOF arm has its own mass — the scene extractor binds
  -- this per entity, not as a global value
  --
  -- affects:
  --   moment-of-inertia: I = (1/3)·m·L²  (rod about proximal end)
  --   gravitational torque: τ_grav = m·g·L/2·cos(θ_world)
  --   Newton-Euler dynamics: inertia matrix coupling between joints
  --
  -- in the chala-apeksha model: the mass of link[i] contributes to the
  -- torque required at joint[j] for ALL j ≤ i (every ancestor joint must
  -- support and accelerate this mass)

  "subanta-swarupa"
  "domain-robotics-sthita kinematic-chain-yukta"
  "mass-abheda"
  "link-yukta"
  "kilogram-matra"
  "moment-of-inertia-yukta torque-yukta"

